<v Harmon Leon>[《Juiced》主题曲]

00:13:36.080 --> 00:14:04.610
<v Nancy Updike>Incredibly, this exists. It was a one-time special on Pay Per View. Just one episode, about an hour long. And I've got the DVD on my desk right now. Here's the description on the cover. Quote, "witness O.J. Simpson performing hilarious practical jokes and shocking hidden camera stunts on unsuspecting real life people all across America. No one is safe, because the juice is loose again."
<v Nancy Updike>令人难以置信的是，它确实存在。这是一个在按次付费电视(Pay Per View)上播放的特别节目。只有一集，大约一个小时长。我的桌子上现在就有这张DVD。封面上是这样描述的。引用：“亲眼见证O.J. Simpson在全美范围内对毫无防备的普通人进行搞笑的恶作剧和令人震惊的隐藏摄像机特技。没有人是安全的，因为Juice又放出来了。”

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:30.200
<v Nancy Updike>My first question when I saw it was, why does this exist? Which is a dumb question. Reality shows exist because they're cheap to make and people watch them. Maybe a better question is, why isn't this hidden camera prank show from 2006 as well known and scrutinized as every other part of O.J. Simpson's public life? I'm here to say, I think it's worth a look.
<v Nancy Updike>我看到它时的第一个问题是，这东西为什么存在？这是个愚蠢的问题。真人秀的存在是因为制作成本低，而且有人看。也许更好的问题是，为什么这个2006年的隐藏摄像机恶作剧节目不像O.J. Simpson公众生活的其他部分那样广为人知并受到审视？我在这里想说，我认为它值得一看。

00:14:30.200 --> 00:15:01.990
<v Nancy Updike>Here's a show that was never meant to be taken seriously. And because of that, we get these strange, revealing glimpses of O.J. Goofing around in front of the camera, chatting with strangers, riffing. It's an hour with him unlike any hour you've ever seen. I also think it might be the most mystifying celebrity comeback vehicle ever made.
<v Nancy Updike>这是一档从未打算认真对待的节目。正因如此，我们得以看到O.J.一些奇怪而深刻的片段。他在摄像机前胡闹，与陌生人聊天，即兴发挥。这是你见过的最不像任何其他节目的一个小时。我还认为这可能是历史上最令人费解的名人复出工具。

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:24.510
<v Nancy Updike>The show is a whole bunch of short prank scenarios, one after another, in different locations-- fast food place, golf course, bingo parlor. Sometimes O.J. is in disguise. Sometimes he's not. The idea was O.J. Would be someplace doing something, and Harmon's job was to help piss off the people around him. Or in prank show lingo--
<v Nancy Updike>节目是由一连串短暂的恶作剧场景组成的，地点各不相同——快餐店、高尔夫球场、宾果游戏厅。有时O.J.戴着伪装。有时没有。构思是O.J.会在某个地方做某事，而Harmon的工作是帮助激怒周围的人。或者用恶作剧节目的行话来说——

